      "content": "right, so it basically sounds like the \"opposition\" is just making noise about old-school stuff while the real experts are moving toward UBI. if the automation is truly inevitable, isn't it kind of reductive to even debate the \"cost\" when the cost of doing nothing is basically a total societal collapse? it feels like we're past the point where the fiscal conservative arguments even matter anymore.",
